# uc-coding — coding sampling, on a decensored model instead of stock weights.
#
# This is `coding` with the model swapped: every sampler value below is
# byte-for-byte what modes/coding.env sets (Qwen3.8's published thinking-mode
# preset, every creative sampler at llama.cpp's disabled value, THINK_LANG=zh).
# The ONLY difference from coding is MODEL_REPO/GGUF_FILE. If you change a
# sampler here, change it in coding.env too, or the two coding regimes drift.
#
# QUALIFIED 2026-09-02: that is true of THIS FILE and false of the behaviour.
# Swapping the GGUF also swaps the chat template baked into it, and the two are
# not the same template — coding's unsloth GGUF carries a 9993-char fork,
# this one carries Qwen's published 8952-char original. They disagree about
# which request shapes are legal: `reasoning_effort=high`, a second leading
# system message, and a `developer` role all render under coding and all return
# HTTP 500 here. Measured, not read off a card:
# context/design/the-template-is-part-of-the-model.md, reproduce with
# scripts/template_probe.py. So "same sampling, different weights" is right,
# and "same regime" is not.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHICH MODEL, and the decision that is deferred.
#
# Three decensored 3.8 builds are documented in this repo (fuller comparison of
# the older two in modes/prose.env). They sit at different points and the choice
# is REAL:
#
#   orcarouter/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored (own Q4_K_M) — SET BELOW, 2026-08-25.
#     The best-evidenced of the three, and the first one whose capability cost
#     is small enough to belong in a CODING regime.
#
#     VERIFIED HERE off the Hub before selection, by the same three checks
#     modes/prose.env demands after the OBLITERATUS source GGUF passed its card
#     and then failed the smoke test (scripts/gguf_probe.py, run against
#     mradermacher's i1-Q4_K_M as a control — it reproduced prose.env's recorded
#     8952 / 866 / 16,810,715,616 exactly):
#       chat template  8952 chars, tools=T tool_call=T reasoning_effort=T
#                      thinking=T   <- the check that rejected the last candidate
#       MTP            866 tensors, block_count=65, nextn_predict_layers=1,
#                      blk.64.nextn.{eh_proj,enorm,hnorm,shared_head_norm}
#       size           16,810,714,496 B — within 1.1 kB of the OBLITERATED
#                      Q4_K_M it replaces, so VRAM headroom is unchanged
#
#     Evals are the AUTHOR'S, from the model card: measured on this exact
#     abliterated build against Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8 with the same scripts.
#       MMLU 0-shot   84.3 -> 84.7  (+0.4)     GSM8K CoT   90.0 -> 88.7  (-1.3)
#       MMLU-Pro CoT  77.6 -> 76.8  (-0.8)     CMMLU       81.4 -> 80.8  (-0.6)
#       harmful-prompt refusal 64-99% -> 0-6%, and benign over-refusal falls too
#     Refusal is published for thinking ON as well as OFF, which matters here
#     because this stack runs thinking mode — the other two cards do not split it.
#
#     Read those numbers with three caveats, none of them small. They are the
#     author's own, not reproduced on this box. The n is small (300/250/150/500).
#     The refusal judge is a rule-based opening-phrase classifier, which
#     over-credits a model that refuses in an unusual register. And they are NOT
#     comparable with the OBLITERATUS figures below, which come from a different
#     source against a different baseline — do not read 84.7 vs 82.3 as a
#     head-to-head.
#
#     GATED on the Hub (`gated: auto`): accept the terms once on the model page,
#     then the fetch needs HF_TOKEN, which lives in .env.local (gitignored) and
#     reaches the downloader through docker-compose.yml. Without it the download
#     fails 401/403, which does not look like an auth problem from the log.
#
#     NOT established: whether this fixes the degenerate repetition loop that
#     prompted the swap. That loop was reproduced on the OBLITERATED weights and
#     is the REASON for the change, but no measurement here shows the new model
#     is free of it. Re-run the replay in the loop probe before claiming it.
#
#   OBLITERATUS/Qwen3.8-27B-OBLITERATED (mradermacher i1-Q4_K_M) — PREVIOUS.
#     Shares the prose model — the same GGUF backs both — so uc-coding needed no
#     extra download, which is the only reason it started here. (The source
#     repo's OWN Q4_K_M was tried on 2026-08-26 and rejected: it bakes a stripped
#     chat template with no tool-calling support, which breaks native function
#     calling — the one thing a CODING regime most needs. mradermacher's i1
#     requant of the same V3 weights carries the full Qwen3 tool template. Full
#     autopsy in modes/prose.env.) Removes soft "safety-lecture" deflections,
#     not just hard refusals. BUT its capability cost is concentrated in STEM:
#     MMLU 84.5 -> 82.3 overall, and -3.3pp in STEM specifically. That is the
#     wrong place to spend capability for a CODING regime, and every other
#     file in this stack (.env, versions.lock, modes/prose.env) says this
#     model must NOT back coding for exactly that reason.
#
#     Moving off it costs the shared-GGUF property: prose still runs these
#     weights, so uc-coding and prose no longer share one file and switching
#     between them is now a full cold reload plus ~16.8 GB more on disk. That is
#     the price of not carrying -3.3pp of STEM into a coding regime. If you would
#     rather have the disk back, the question to ask is whether PROSE should move
#     to orcarouter too — its card reports over-refusal falling as well, which is
#     the axis prose actually selected OBLITERATUS for.
#
#   JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored (IQ4_XS) — THE DOCUMENTED UPGRADE.
#     The repo's own pick for a model that has to serve coding duty: "If one
#     model ever has to serve both regimes, use this one, not OBLITERATUS."
#     Heretic abliteration merged at bf16 (not a quantized round trip).
#     Capability delta MMLU -0.2, mean -0.5 — every delta INSIDE stderr, so
#     STEM is essentially preserved. MTP head grafted back from base and
#     verified. Cost: ~12/100 residual refusals (vs OBLITERATUS's ~0), and it
#     has NEVER been downloaded to this box — a ~15 GB pull.
#
# To promote uc-coding to the JonathanColetti build, download it and paste the
# two lines below over the two active ones:
#
#   MODEL_REPO=JonathanColetti/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
#   GGUF_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-IQ4_XS.gguf
#   # sha256 53adc4bbed67044d662273356bbf3a50fdec667ac21bbf18d13e5815fbccc7f5
#   # 15309039008 bytes
#
# BEWARE the noMTP twins in that repo: it publishes both `X-IQ4_XS.gguf` and
# `X-noMTP-IQ4_XS.gguf`. The noMTP file loads fine and silently kills
# --spec-type draft-mtp. Take the one WITHOUT `noMTP` in the name, and confirm
# the GGUF header off the Hub before download: 866 tensors, block_count=65,
# nextn_predict_layers=1, blk.64.nextn.* all four present.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Sampling: identical to coding. Qwen3.8-27B card, thinking mode "Best
# Practices" — temperature=1.0, top_p=0.95, top_k=20, min_p=0.0,
# presence_penalty=0.0, repetition_penalty=1.0. Every creative sampler off.

MODEL_REPO=orcarouter/Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-GGUF
GGUF_FILE=Qwen3.8-27B-Uncensored-Q4_K_M.gguf
# sha256 3445102e9cde5d562508642c100a2f5ac3368a5a3f748442811d7a95daee3bec
# 16810714496 bytes

TEMPERATURE=1.0
TOP_P=0.95
TOP_K=20
MIN_P=0.0

PRESENCE_PENALTY=0.0
FREQUENCY_PENALTY=0.0
REPEAT_PENALTY=1.0
REPEAT_LAST_N=64

DRY_MULTIPLIER=0.0
XTC_PROBABILITY=0.0
DYNATEMP_RANGE=0.0
TOP_N_SIGMA=-1.0

# Thinking depth. medium injects no steering sentence; xhigh (upstream default)
# does not fit a 4096-token reasoning budget. Same as coding.
REASONING_EFFORT=medium

# Chat template. Empty = use the one baked into this mode's GGUF, which is the
# only combination any measurement in this repo was taken against.
#
# It is declared in EVERY mode file on purpose. scripts/mode.sh only rewrites
# keys the target mode names, so a key set in one mode and absent from another
# SURVIVES the switch — and this one is model-coupled: carrying coding's
# unsloth template into prose would silently render orcarouter's weights under
# another model's prompt format, with no line in mode.sh's output saying so.
# Declaring it empty here makes every switch reset it.
# See the CHAT_TEMPLATE_FILE block in .env.
CHAT_TEMPLATE_FILE=

# Reasoning in Mandarin, as coding sets it. Kept identical so uc-coding differs
# from coding in exactly one axis, the model. THINK_LANG is the reasoning-
# language fragment (verbatim tool args, code identifiers); it is steering for
# an agentic coding session, not a filter, and it is the right default here.
THINK_LANG=zh
